Tune Lad identification sidecar

This directory contains code from other projects, kept under their own licences:

- engine/ (except engine/vendor/): the recognition engine of Cadence, https://github.com/Batpapa/Cadence,
  commit 90149e9df40a180dd2c7bd832707bc4e405102ae, copyright its authors, licensed under the GNU Affero General
  Public License version 3 or later (engine/LICENSE). Only the files the engine imports were copied, unchanged.
- engine/vendor/folkfriend/: FolkFriend by Tom Wyllie, https://github.com/TomWyllie/folkfriend, as built in Cadence's
  fork (https://github.com/Batpapa/folkfriend), licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 only
  (engine/vendor/folkfriend/LICENSE).
- engine/vendor/cadence-transcriptor/: the note decoder's analysis of Cadence compiled to WebAssembly (from the
  `transcriptor/rust` sources of the Cadence repository), AGPL-3.0-or-later.

src/ is Tune Lad's own wrapper and shares the licence of this repository (GPL-3.0). The sidecar runs as its own
container and talks to the application over HTTP only. The corresponding source of everything in it is this directory;
users of the running service can get it from the repository (AGPL section 13).

The tune index the sidecar downloads at start comes from https://github.com/TomWyllie/folkfriend-app-data, which is
built from thesession.org data.
